  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "MCP-Manager",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n`@mcp-manager/mcp-manager` — a **dual-face Model Context Protocol manager plugin** for [deepseek-harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) (dsh, built on [Cordis](https://cordis.js.org)). Single package, two entry points, one composition row: the Host half supervises any number of MCP servers, while the browser half renders a service management panel and a JSON configuration editor."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Board View**: Card-based UI for adding, editing, and managing MCP servers with one-click operations\n- **JSON View**: Direct JSON configuration editor for power users\n- **MCP Market**: Browse and install popular MCP servers from [mcp-cn.com](https://www.mcp-cn.com/) with one click\n- **Connection Testing**: Test server connections with step-by-step results before saving\n- **Health Check**: Per-server health monitoring with detailed diagnostic output\n- **Multiple Transports**: Supports stdio, HTTP, SSE, and Streamable HTTP\n- **Headers Editor**: Postman-style row-based editor for HTTP headers\n- **Delete Confirmation**: Two-step confirmation to prevent accidental deletions\n- **Host-side HTTP Proxy**: Market API requests go through Node.js to bypass browser CORS restrictions"
    },
    {
      "section": "Version compatibility",
      "text": "`@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` `0.1.5-rc.2` lockstep line or newer (see `package.json` peer dependencies)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add @mcp-manager/mcp-manager\n```\n\nRestart `dsh web`, then open **Settings → MCP**. The install auto-inserts the composition row; the panel appears as its own sidebar entry."
    },
    {
      "section": "List View",
      "text": "The default view shows all configured MCP servers with their live status (connecting / ready / failed / disabled), tool count, and quick controls:\n\n- **Expand**: Show/hide the server's registered tools\n- **Restart**: Reconnect the server\n- **Delete**: Remove the server (with confirmation)\n- **Enable/Disable**: Toggle the server on/off"
    },
    {
      "section": "Board View",
      "text": "Click **\"Configure MCP\"** to enter the board view. Each server is rendered as a card with:\n\n- Enable/disable toggle\n- Edit (pencil) button\n- Delete (trash) button with two-step confirmation\n- Health check (pulse) button\n\nUse **\"+ Add Server\"** to create a new server entry. The form supports:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Board View",
      "text": "- Transport type selection (stdio / HTTP / SSE / Streamable HTTP)\n- Command + arguments for stdio\n- URL + headers for HTTP-type servers\n- Environment variables (one per line)\n- **Test Connection** button to verify the server before saving"
    },
    {
      "section": "JSON View",
      "text": "Switch to the JSON tab to edit the raw `mcp.json` configuration directly."
    },
    {
      "section": "Market",
      "text": "Switch to the Market tab to browse popular MCP servers from [mcp-cn.com](https://www.mcp-cn.com/). Features:\n\n- Search by keyword\n- Infinite scroll pagination\n- Server logo, tags, and usage count\n- One-click add to pre-fill the board form"
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "One npm package exposes two entry points:\n\n| Entry | Plane | Responsibility |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.` | Host (Node) | Supervises MCP connections from `~/.dsh/mcp.json` (stdio / http / sse / streamable-http, tool discovery, auto-reconnect); exposes the `mcp` Remote namespace including `fetchMarket` for CORS-free market API access. |\n| `./client` | Client (web) | MCP service panel + board view + JSON editor + market browser, injected into `settings.section`. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "**Host face**: `McpRegistry` (extends `TypertRemoteService`) layers entry config over `mcp.json` user config, then hands the result to an internal `ServerSupervisor` — one connection per server, re-creating only what changed. Tools register under `mcp__<serverName>__` on `ctx.tools`. The `fetchMarket` method proxies HTTP requests to external APIs on behalf of the client, avoiding browser CORS restrictions."
    },
    {
      "section": "Architecture",
      "text": "**Client face**: `apply` self-mounts the `mcp` Remote namespace, creates a `McpManagerController`, and injects the panel into `settings.section`. All RPC calls are serialized on a single queue to prevent concurrent answer clobbering."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
